The paper is an attempt to characterize performance profile of intel meteor lake processor for graph, attention, and deep Neural Net. AI models using intel's OpenVINO code-to-hardware mapper. The results mostly boil down to numerous limitations of the hardware that only supports int8 and fp32 precisions and mostly fails due to the lack of supporting the hardware for the tested workloads. Majority of the selected benchmarks and datasets date back a decade ago.

Due to an old datasets and models, and the low-end hardware used in the tests, I failed to appreciate the contribution of this work to the community at large.

Intel Meteor Lake form factor is low-end CPU and this should be mentioned so that the expectations on the impact and applicability are set accordingly.

Please define npu in text, not just in the abstract.

For most technical writing, spmm is sparse matrix multiply, And spdmm is sparse-times-dense matrix multiply.

What is ref. #4, 6, 7? They are generic links that require the reader to do deep involvement in finding the actual information.

What (and why) loading is isolated in a subprocess and how things change when no isolation occurs? This is quick remark that requires more explanation since loading is essential of any code dealing with datasets. See this sentence:

Dataset loading is isolated in a subprocess to
prevent environment conflicts.

What is latency in IV.A? How does it relate to other performance metrics?

Why does the notation change from Gpu to iGpu throughout the text?

What is purpose of dot in '(.failed marker)'? Why not just call it 'failed'? Most of the '.failed' markers are nowhere to be find in tables or figures.

The point of Fig. 3 is doubtful since most of time is spent in 'other' category, which is not explained.

Fig. 4 is a heatmap but only green is present on the graph with only one small red dot. What information does it convey?
